1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,128
In this town, nothing stays lost.

2
00:00:02,793 --> 00:00:05,468
Everything you lose ends up in one place.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:07,822
The Lost and Found.

4
00:00:08,293 --> 00:00:10,968
A huge building in the center of town.

5
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:13,928
Lost keys. Lost socks. Lost homework.

6
00:00:14,593 --> 00:00:15,752
Even lost dogs.

7
00:00:16,393 --> 00:00:19,674
You just walk in, find your stuff, and walk out.

8
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,222
Mister Finch runs it.

9
00:00:22,693 --> 00:00:25,065
He has worked there for sixty years.

10
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,625
He knows where everything is.

11
00:00:28,193 --> 00:00:30,262
Last week, I lost my backpack.

12
00:00:30,927 --> 00:00:33,601
So I went to the Lost and Found.

13
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:35,652
Aisle twelve. Backpacks.

14
00:00:36,293 --> 00:00:38,058
Right next to aisle thirteen.

15
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:39,483
Lost time.

16
00:00:40,427 --> 00:00:42,192
Jars full of glowing minutes.

17
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,434
"Lost when you were bored," the labels said.

18
00:00:46,327 --> 00:00:47,183
Aisle fourteen.

19
00:00:48,127 --> 00:00:48,996
Lost memories.

20
00:00:49,927 --> 00:00:50,783
Aisle fifteen.

21
00:00:51,727 --> 00:00:52,583
Lost voices.

22
00:00:53,527 --> 00:00:55,292
And at the very end...

23
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:56,716
aisle sixteen.

24
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:58,516
Lost people.

25
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:00,922
Shelves of sleeping kids.

26
00:01:01,393 --> 00:01:02,552
Hundreds of them.

27
00:01:03,193 --> 00:01:05,565
Each with a tag on their wrist.

28
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,428
One of them was my brother.

29
00:01:09,093 --> 00:01:11,162
Except my brother is at home.

30
00:01:11,827 --> 00:01:12,683
Eating dinner.

31
00:01:13,627 --> 00:01:14,483
Right now.

32
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:17,192
I ran to Mister Finch.

33
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,131
"Who's that at my house?" I asked.

34
00:01:20,927 --> 00:01:21,783
He smiled.

35
00:01:22,727 --> 00:01:24,795
"Whatever the town finds..." he said.

36
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,619
"it gives back."

37
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:29,328
"Even if it isn't the same."

38
00:01:29,993 --> 00:01:32,971
That night, my brother asked me where I'd been.

39
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,331
I told him the Lost and Found.

40
00:01:37,127 --> 00:01:38,286
He stopped smiling.

41
00:01:38,927 --> 00:01:40,995
"Don't go back there," he whispered.

42
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,425
"They're running out of shelves."

